    "['interface [interface_name] virtual-circuit-id [vc_id]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'l2vpn xconnect context PE2_PE1', 'parent_command': ['neighbor [parameter1] activate'], 'root': 'neighbor [parameter1] activate', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco configuration command for the Juniper L2Circuit configuration:\\n\\n##\\nl2vpn xconnect context PE2_PE1\\n member GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1\\n neighbor 1.1.1.1 100 encapsulation mpls\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco IOS XE/XR, this creates an L2VPN cross-connect context where:\\n- `PE2_PE1` is a locally significant name for the connection\\n- `GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1` is the local interface\\n- `1.1.1.1` is the remote LDP router ID\\n- `100` is the virtual circuit ID\\n- `mpls` specifies the encapsulation type (equivalent to Juniper's default MPLS encapsulation for L2circuit)\", 'trans_template': 'l2vpn xconnect context PE2_PE1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'member GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1', 'parent_command': ['neighbor [parameter1] activate'], 'root': 'neighbor [parameter1] activate', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco configuration command for the Juniper L2Circuit configuration:\\n\\n##\\nl2vpn xconnect context PE2_PE1\\n member GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1\\n neighbor 1.1.1.1 100 encapsulation mpls\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco IOS XE/XR, this creates an L2VPN cross-connect context where:\\n- `PE2_PE1` is a locally significant name for the connection\\n- `GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1` is the local interface\\n- `1.1.1.1` is the remote LDP router ID\\n- `100` is the virtual circuit ID\\n- `mpls` specifies the encapsulation type (equivalent to Juniper's default MPLS encapsulation for L2circuit)\", 'trans_template': 'member GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 1.1.1.1 100 encapsulation mpls', 'parent_command': ['neighbor [parameter1] activate'], 'root': 'neighbor [parameter1] activate', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco configuration command for the Juniper L2Circuit configuration:\\n\\n##\\nl2vpn xconnect context PE2_PE1\\n member GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1\\n neighbor 1.1.1.1 100 encapsulation mpls\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco IOS XE/XR, this creates an L2VPN cross-connect context where:\\n- `PE2_PE1` is a locally significant name for the connection\\n- `GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1` is the local interface\\n- `1.1.1.1` is the remote LDP router ID\\n- `100` is the virtual circuit ID\\n- `mpls` specifies the encapsulation type (equivalent to Juniper's default MPLS encapsulation for L2circuit)\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 1.1.1.1 100 encapsulation mpls'}]]": 1,
    "['interface [parameter2] encapsulation-type [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'l2vpn xconnect context PE2-PE1', 'parent_command': ['neighbor [parameter1] activate'], 'root': 'neighbor [parameter1] activate', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco command for the Juniper L2Circuit configuration:\\n\\n##\\nl2vpn xconnect context PE2-PE1\\n member GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1\\n neighbor 1.1.1.1 100 encapsulation ethernet\\n##\\n\\nThis Cisco configuration:\\n1. Creates an L2VPN cross-connect context\\n2. Specifies the local interface (equivalent to ge-1/0/1.1)\\n3. Points to the neighbor (1.1.1.1) with the same VC ID (100)\\n4. Sets the encapsulation type to Ethernet (matching the Juniper command)\", 'trans_template': 'l2vpn xconnect context PE2-PE1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'member GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1', 'parent_command': ['neighbor [parameter1] activate'], 'root': 'neighbor [parameter1] activate', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco command for the Juniper L2Circuit configuration:\\n\\n##\\nl2vpn xconnect context PE2-PE1\\n member GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1\\n neighbor 1.1.1.1 100 encapsulation ethernet\\n##\\n\\nThis Cisco configuration:\\n1. Creates an L2VPN cross-connect context\\n2. Specifies the local interface (equivalent to ge-1/0/1.1)\\n3. Points to the neighbor (1.1.1.1) with the same VC ID (100)\\n4. Sets the encapsulation type to Ethernet (matching the Juniper command)\", 'trans_template': 'member GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 1.1.1.1 100 encapsulation ethernet', 'parent_command': ['neighbor [parameter1] activate'], 'root': 'neighbor [parameter1] activate', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco command for the Juniper L2Circuit configuration:\\n\\n##\\nl2vpn xconnect context PE2-PE1\\n member GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1\\n neighbor 1.1.1.1 100 encapsulation ethernet\\n##\\n\\nThis Cisco configuration:\\n1. Creates an L2VPN cross-connect context\\n2. Specifies the local interface (equivalent to ge-1/0/1.1)\\n3. Points to the neighbor (1.1.1.1) with the same VC ID (100)\\n4. Sets the encapsulation type to Ethernet (matching the Juniper command)\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 1.1.1.1 100 encapsulation ethernet'}]]": 1,
